          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Summary: Successive observations at 5-minute intervals of the silent passage across the night sky of 3 red-orange light phenomena: likely observations of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "2913b88b45eb1518409841461d309e40cd8c58a6023b30a20589e36230d0efac"
        },
        {
          "end_ms": null,
          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-646386832e2f2df2f96ac6fe",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-834cc076f2f56f493c0e3135",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-834cc076f2f56f493c0e3135",
          "source_text_sha256": "a323c4f7ddf858b9503bac87b7d65da06b70d463b74a21602587a0b890af15d2",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On June 16, 2019 (not June 15, as incorrectly indicated in the questionnaire) between 12:15 AM and 12:30 AM, a witness observed the successive, 5-minute intervals of three identical red-orange light phenomena passing quickly and silently. The witness reports, \"No precise shape, rather an intense light like a red-orange fireball.\" He sends us a link to the video taken. Only one testimony is collected. The hypotheses of a star Capella or an airplane remain too unlikely to be considered (see the investigation report). On the other hand, considering the defined elements, such as: - the estimated speed of the PAN in motion, exceeding that of an airplane,\n- the repetition of the phenomenon, namely 3 times at intervals of a few minutes,\n- the description of the PAN and analysis of its characteristics (color, shape, brightness, disappearance, etc.) via the video and IPACO software. Here is the translation of the provided GEIPAN text:\n\nIt is necessary to emphasize the very rapid light fluctuation observed in the video as well as the progressive disappearance. These are very important details: the trajectory of the observed phenomenon corresponding to the direction of the wind, and remaining a key criterion of this analysis, and to conclude, the fact that this observation took place on a summer Saturday night, a time conducive to festive events, we can therefore determine that this observation most certainly concerns the observation of Thai lanterns at intervals of a few minutes. These objects were, moreover, much closer to the witness than he thought (probably due to a very cloudy sky) and thus gave him the impression of high speed. This case is to be classified as \"B\" for a very probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "60e695a94bf153c8e346a22ef0fc551a35dd847714cb00c2c528a4ce1f142cae"
        }
      ],
